WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
A new study shows natural forest regrowth delivers carbon and biodiversity gains at up to 96% lower cost than tree planting. This is Planetterrian Daily, episode 158. A University of Queensland and University of Newcastle analysis compared natural regeneration with active tree planting programs. Natural regrowth achieved comparable carbon storage and species recovery at up to 96% lower cost. The study used field data

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:55.100
from multiple tropical and temperate sites results support policy shifts toward protecting regrowth areas rather than uniform planting. Monitoring will continue to assess long-term stability under changing climate conditions. Now, shifting to cellular level interactions inside the body. A review in cell examine the how immune cells and brain tissue interact across multiple neurodegenerative conditions.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:01:13.940
The work highlights pathways where peripheral immune signals reach the central nervous system and influence neuronal health. Researchers note that these interactions vary by disease stage and brain region. The analysis draws on recent single cell and imaging data to clarify which immune populations participate.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:40.760
Follow-up studies are expected to test whether modulating specific immune brain interfaces alters disease progression. On a different note, research into algae strains that bind and remove microplastic particles from water. Science Friday highlights research into algae strains that bind and remove microplastic particles from water. The approach uses the algae's natural surface properties to capture plastic fragments without added chemicals.

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:53.300
Early tests show the algae can be harvested after binding, offering a potential low energy removal step. The work focuses on common freshwater and marine species already present in many ecosystems.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:02:08.520
Next steps include scaling the method to larger water volumes and checking effects on other aquatic organisms. Researchers at the University of Olu developed a spatial accessibility model that links food supply to demand across transport systems.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:23.620
The framework incorporates economic inequality and disruption scenarios to show where supply chains break down. Results indicate that physical distance alone does not determine access, cost barriers and network gaps matter more in many regions.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:36.080
The team combined global trade data with road and port maps to run the simulations. Future applications include testing how targeted infrastructure changes could improve food security under climate stress.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:44.780
A study published in Nature Communications analyzed fossil records to track diversity changes in large African herbivores over time.

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:53.460
The loss of species weighing more than one ton resulted mainly from low rates of new species formation rather than elevated extinction.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:03:06.000
The team from MNCN-CSIC, C-E-N-I-E-H and the University of Alkalaw compared speciation and extinction metrics across geological intervals.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:11.140
Results challenge earlier views that these animals were simply more extinction prone.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:16.960
The work helps explain current ecosystem engineering gaps left by elephants and hippopotamuses.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:25.900
A University of Sheffield study measured grass biomass response to elevated atmospheric carbon dioxide in water-limited savannah plots.

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:31.400
Grasses showed increased growth rates under higher CO2 even when water was scarce.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:38.820
The findings suggest that ongoing atmospheric change could alter vegetation structure and fire regimes in these ecosystems.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:49.060
Data were collected across multiple sites with controlled CO2 exposure. Researchers will track whether the extra growth persists under combined heat and drought stress.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:59.480
Simulations from Helmholtz's centrum here on indicate that extensive offshore wind expansion could increase precipitation over the sea while reducing it near coasts.

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:04.880
The model accounts for changes in surface roughness and heat flux is caused by turbine arrays.

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:10.040
Effects appear only under the most ambitious 2050 build out scenarios.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:14.880
The study focuses on the North Sea region targeted by European Union targets.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:19.680
Further modeling will examine impacts on agriculture and freshwater supply.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:27.780
Cornell engineers created a virtual replica of urban carbon dioxide conditions using sensor networks and fluid dynamics.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:33.820
The system updates in real time and identifies emission hotspots without physical site visits.

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:38.460
Planners can test intervention scenarios in the model before deployment.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:45.960
The framework combines traffic, building, and meteorological data. Expansion to other cities is under discussion.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:58.160
From cleaning physical environments to cleaning up scattered research data, an AI system scanned hundreds of research papers to identify new lead-free materials that retain performance at high temperatures.

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:04.180
The method converts scattered experimental results into structured data for rapid comparison.

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:08.880
Several candidate compounds emerged that had not been tested together before.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:16.460
The study demonstrates how text mining can shift materials discovery from trial and error toward data-driven selection.

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:21.000
Researchers plan laboratory validation of the top predicted materials.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:28.960
Research cleared two technical barriers that previously limited single element metal lenses for augmented and virtual reality glasses.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:33.980
The new structures maintain image quality while reducing overall lens thickness.

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:39.960
Performance tests showed improved color fidelity and reduced aberrations at wide fields of view.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:44.720
The approach replaces stacked conventional lenses with one engineered surface.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:50.060
Continued development aims at full-color prototypes suitable for wearable devices.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:59.420
Researchers at MPIK Heidelberg used an atomic gas as a time-dependent optical element to manipulate XUV and X-ray pulses.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.500
The method allows spectral and temporal control without solid state damage limits.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:10.560
Test demonstrated pulse compression and shaping at intensities relevant to chemical reaction studies.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:14.880
The approach could support quantum computing and advanced spectroscopy.

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:18.160
Further work will scale the technique to shorter wavelengths.

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:24.020
Julie Ellie at Berkeley mapped vocalizations used by flock members outside of song.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:30.700
The work distinguishes contact calls, alarm signals, and coordination sounds that occur throughout the day.

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:36.020
Recordings from multiple species revealed consistent patterns tied to social context.

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:42.260
The findings expand understanding of avian communication beyond courtship and territory defense.

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:47.920
Ongoing experiments test how birds respond to playbacks of specific chatter types.

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:51.560
From engineered materials to human systems under stress.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:59.180
A doctoral study found that declining occupational well-being often leads to sick leave without changes at the job site itself.

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:03.880
Mental health issues now rank as the leading cause of absence in Finland.

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:10.620
The research shows that individual support alone does not address root causes tied to workload and environment.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:14.600
Data came from national health registers and workplace records.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:20.240
The findings point to the need for organizational level interventions alongside personal care.

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:23.740
From human health data to cellular aging signals.

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:33.280
Cohort and mouse data connect the circulating factor ANG-PTL-8 produced by aged fat cells to inflammation and mortality risk.

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:39.300
Higher levels correlated with several age-associated conditions in both humans and the animal model.

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:43.800
The study identifies senescent adipocytes as a source of this signal.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:50.660
Removing or inhibiting the cells lowered ANG-PTL-8 and improved metabolic markers in mice.

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:56.700
Human follow-up will test whether ANG-PTL-8 serves as a practical biomarker.

00:07:57.300 --> 00:08:01.940
A few episodes back the show covered cellular aging markers in longevity biology.

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:06.880
Today's work adds a specific circulating factor tied to senescent fat cells.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:11.960
Now, here's something most people get wrong about how wound clots actually form.

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:20.320
Most people picture fibrinogen as a simple dissolved protein that turns into solid fibrin strands the moment it meets air at a cut.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:23.300
The actual process is more staged.

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:25.820
Right now, as blood leaves a vessel,

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:34.980
fibrinogen molecules first adsorb onto the exposed surface in a specific orientation that was only clarified after years of experiments.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:44.160
The revised model shows the protein rearranges into a denser layer before thrombin converts it to fibrin, changing how the clot mesh assembles.

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:52.880
One memorable detail is that the surface confirmation shift takes place within seconds, faster than many standard clotting assays capture.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:58.240
This matters because current wound dressings and sealants were designed around the older view.

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:06.500
A practical step is to watch for updated guidelines on topical agents once clinical labs test materials match to the new structure.

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:13.240
Keep an eye on follow-up work testing whether modulating immune brain interfaces alters disease progression.

